ifications_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jbaldwin/liblifthttp/notifications{?since,all,participating}","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jbaldwin/liblifthttp/labels{/name}","releases_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jbaldwin/liblifthttp/releases{/id}","deployments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jbaldwin/liblifthttp/deployments","created_at":"2017-07-09T00:05:55Z","updated_at":"2025-12-12T15:11:01Z","pushed_at":"2025-12-12T15:10:56Z","git_url":"git://github.com/jbaldwin/liblifthttp.git","ssh_url":"git@github.com:jbaldwin/liblifthttp.git","clone_url":"https://github.com/jbaldwin/liblifthttp.git","svn_url":"https://github.com/jbaldwin/liblifthttp","homepage":"","size":839,"stargazers_count":71,"watchers_count":71,"language":"C++","has_issues":true,"has_projects":true,"has_downloads":true,"has_wiki":true,"has_pages":false,"has_discussions":false,"forks_count":24,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":3,"license":{"key":"other","name":"Other","spdx_id":"NOASSERTION","url":null,"node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTA="},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"topics":["async","asynchronous","cpp","cpp17","cpp17-library","curl","event-driven","http-client","modern-cpp","uv"],"visibility":"public","forks":24,"open_issues":3,"watchers":71,"default_branch":"main","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"body":"I'm almost 100% that the exact same version of lift (it hasn't been modified in a while after all) did work earlier this year, so it might be something that has changed with libcurl. Its changelog during that time is quite extensive so it will take a while to sift through...\r\n\r\nRunning the `lift_async_simple` example now segfaults.\r\n```\r\n(gdb) bt -entry-values both\r\n#0  0x00007ffff7f3cccf in ?? () from /lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/libcurl-nss.so.4\r\n#1  0x00007ffff7f3d222 in ?? () from /lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/libcurl-nss.so.4\r\n#2  0x00007ffff7f3d3bf in curl_multi_socket_action () from /lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/libcurl-nss.so.4\r\n#3  0x00005555555c7999 in lift::client::check_actions (this=0x7fffffffd390, \r\n    this@entry=<optimized out>, socket=-1, socket@entry=<optimized out>, event_bitmask=0, \r\n    event_bitmask@entry=<optimized out>) at /home/andjonss/devel/liblifthttp/src/client.cpp:235\r\n#4  0x00005555555c7944 in lift::client::check_actions (this=0x7fffffffd390, \r\n    this@entry=<optimized out>) at /home/andjonss/devel/liblifthttp/src/client.cpp:226\r\n#5  0x00005555555c87ee in lift::curl_start_timeout (timeout_ms=0, timeout_ms@entry=<optimized out>, \r\n    user_data=0x7fffffffd390, user_data@entry=<optimized out>)\r\n    at /home/andjonss/devel/liblifthttp/src/client.cpp:506\r\n\r\n```\r\nThe top of the stack trace:\r\n\r\n- The timer callback function `curl_start_timeout` (set in `lift::client` ctor) gets called with a `timeout_ms` of zero, which I understand is normal.\r\n-  For the 0 case it just calls `client::check_actions()` which just unconditionally calls `check_actions(CURL_SOCKET_TIMEOUT, 0)`, where `CURL_SOCKET_TIMEOUT` is -1.\r\n- Here, the received socket (-1) is used in: `curl_code = curl_multi_socket_action(m_cmh, socket, event_bitmask, &running_handles)`, which segfaults.\r\n\r\nI did notice, however, that the docs for CURLMOPT_TIMERFUNCTION does state:\r\n\r\n> WARNING: do not call libcurl directly from within the callback itself when the timeout_ms value is zero,\r\n\r\nWhich lift seems to be doing by calling `client::check_actions()` which eventually calls `curl_multi_socket_action(...)`.\r\n\r\nAnd... is this still being maintained in some capacity?","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jbaldwin/liblifthttp/issues/142/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jbaldwin/liblifthttp/issues/142/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed"}},"event":"cross-referenced"}]